# M5's done-when test, second half: a user page fault reaches its
# fault-handler thread, which prints it and kills the faulting thread
# (user/root/src/fault.rs). The kernel starts the root task with
# test=fault. It retypes two endpoints, E for faults and D for reports, and
# two TCBs: the handler H at priority 200, with an IPC buffer in the second
# KiB of the root task's buffer frame (TCB_SetIPCBuffer), and F at 100,
# whose fault endpoint is a copy of E with only Write and GrantReply. H
# waits on E; F reads 0xdeadbee8, which nothing maps. H checks the VMFault
# message word by word (ip on F's one-instruction read, the address, no
# fetch, a user-mode read of a page not present), reads F's registers
# through its own buffer, and kills F with TCB_Suspend, which cancels the
# fault IPC and deletes the reply capability: H's Reply with label 0 then
# restarts nothing. The root reads F's registers again, drops below F's
# priority and spins for 50 ms: F must stay stopped, or it would fault
# again and H would fail the test.
cmdline: test=fault
exit: success
expect: microL4 kernel
expect: cmdline: "test=fault"
expect: root: microL4 root task
expect: root: cmdline "test=fault"
expect: fault: handler thread H (TCB slot
expect: priority 200, IPC buffer at
expect: fault: thread F (TCB slot
expect: priority 100) has fault endpoint slot
expect: a copy with Write and GrantReply
expect: fault: thread F reads 0xdeadbee8, which nothing maps
expect: fault: handler received VMFault from thread F: ip 0x4 # root_fault_read moves with the image
expect: addr 0xdeadbee8, prefetch 0, fsr 0x4 (a user-mode read of a page not present)
expect: fault: handler read thread F's registers: rip 0x4
expect: is the faulting instruction, rdi 0xdeadbee8
expect: fault: handler killed thread F with TCB_Suspend
expect: fault: root read thread F's registers after the kill: rip 0x4
expect: still the faulting read, rdi 0xdeadbee8
expect: fault: thread F stayed stopped for 50 ms with the root task at priority 50, below its 100
expect: TEST PASS
expect: DEBUG HALT 0 from TCB
